{"id":"b7b984edb0eb40db9cf334384406d59e","model":"gpt-oss-120b","choices":[{"index":0,"message":{"role":"assistant","content":"{\n  \"answer\": \"noanswer\",\n  \"citations\": []\n}","reasoning_content":"We need to answer: \"What United Kingdom Prime Minister was succeeded in the 1990s by the Leader of the Conservative Party?\" The phrasing is ambiguous. Likely asking: Which UK Prime Minister was succeeded (i.e., replaced) in the 1990s by the Leader of the Conservative Party. In the 1990s, the Conservative Party leader became Prime Minister after succeeding a previous PM. In 1990, Margaret Thatcher was succeeded by John Major (who was Conservative Party leader). So the Prime Minister succeeded in the 1990s by the Leader of the Conservative Party: Margaret Thatcher was succeeded by John Major (who was the Conservative Party leader). However the question: \"What United Kingdom Prime Minister was succeeded in the 1990s by the Leader of the Conservative Party?\" Could also refer to John Major succeeded by Tony Blair (Labour) in 1997, but Blair was not Conservative Party leader. So likely answer: Margaret Thatcher.\n\nWe need evidence. Look for evidence about Thatcher being succeeded by John Major in 1990. Not directly in provided evidence. We have evidence about 1997 Conservative Party leadership election triggered when John Major resigned after 1997 election defeat. Also evidence about Federation of Conservative Students etc. Not about Thatcher. We have evidence about Conservative Party (UK) leadership election 1997. Also about Conservative Party being major. But we need citation that Margaret Thatcher was succeeded by John Major in 1990. Not present. Could we infer from \"The 1997 Conservative Party leadership election was triggered ... when John Major resigned ... following his party's defeat at the 1997 general election\". That indicates John Major was leader before 1997. But not about who he succeeded. No evidence about Thatcher.\n\nWe have evidence about \"These were the first annual local elections for the new Conservative Prime Minister Margaret Thatcher.\" That indicates Thatcher was PM in 1980. Not about succession.\n\nWe might need to answer \"noanswer\" if we cannot verify. The question: \"What United Kingdom Prime Minister was succeeded in the 1990s by the Leader of the Conservative Party?\" We need a Prime Minister name. We have evidence that John Major was Conservative Party leader and Prime Minister after Thatcher. But we lack explicit citation that Thatcher was succeeded by Major. However we have evidence that John Major was Conservative leader and Prime Minister until 1997. And we have evidence that Margaret Thatcher was Prime Minister in 1980. Not enough to state succession.\n\nWe could answer \"Margaret Thatcher\" with citation of evidence that she was Prime Minister (1980) and that John Major was Conservative leader (1997). But that doesn't directly show succession. Might be considered insufficient.\n\nBetter to answer \"noanswer\"."},"finish_reason":"stop"}],"usage":{"prompt_tokens":1716,"completion_tokens":581,"total_tokens":2297,"audio_prompt_tokens":0},"created":1791982364,"object":"chat.completion","prompt_filter_results":null}